# --- Git Configuration ---
# The .gitignore file tells Git which files or folders to ignore in the repository.
# Its primary purpose is security: it prevents sensitive information (like API keys)
# from being leaked. It also keeps the project clean by ignoring local,
# temporary, or system-specific files.

# Web site to generate .gitignore file
# https://www.toptal.com/developers/gitignore

# --- Ignored Files ---
# Ensure that sensitive configuration is never pushed to the repository.
.env